<section class="wp-block-group alignfull ok-body"><!-- wp:group {"className":"ok-col","layout":{"type":"default"}} -->
<div class="wp-block-group ok-col"><!-- wp:heading {"level":2,"className":"ok-h2 ok-h2--left ok-col__h"} -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading ok-h2 ok-h2--left ok-col__h">Weekly Rhythm: Floor and Classroom Balance</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"ok-copy"} -->
<p class="ok-copy">The Two-year Diploma in Hotel Operations admits forty-eight students each September, organized into four desk groups of twelve. Our weekly rhythm balances operational practice with academic rigor: students spend three days on the floor of Okami House and two days in class each week. Working in groups of twelve ensures that every student receives direct, personal instruction while managing active floor stations. Classroom days explore hospitality accounting, reservation systems, food safety regulations, and team leadership, directly reinforcing the practical duties performed on hotel shifts. This balanced schedule creates immediate connections between operational reality and hospitality management theory throughout both years.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>
<!-- /wp:group --></section>
<!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:group {"tagName":"section","align":"full","className":"ok-body ok-body--table","layout":{"type":"default"}} -->
<section class="wp-block-group alignfull ok-body ok-body--table"><!-- wp:group {"className":"ok-sechead ok-sechead--left","layout":{"type":"default"}} -->
<div class="wp-block-group ok-sechead ok-sechead--left"><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"ok-label"} -->
<p class="ok-label">PACING</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:heading {"level":2,"className":"ok-h2 ok-h2--left"} -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading ok-h2 ok-h2--left">Four terms at a glance</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading --></div>
<!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:table {"className":"ok-ttable"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-table ok-ttable"><table><tbody><tr><td>Term 1</td><td>Sep–Jan, year one</td><td>Front desk and reservations</td><td>18 weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Term 2</td><td>Feb–Jun, year one</td><td>Banquet and restaurant floor</td><td>18 weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Term 3</td><td>Sep–Jan, year two</td><td>Teaching kitchen and rooms division</td><td>18 weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Term 4</td><td>Feb–Jun, year two</td><td>16-week placement at a partner hotel and a 2-week leadership seminar</td><td>18 weeks</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>
<!-- /wp:table --><!-- wp:group {"className":"ok-col ok-col--after","layout":{"type":"default"}} -->
<div class="wp-block-group ok-col ok-col--after"><!-- wp:heading {"level":2,"anchor":"terms","className":"ok-h2 ok-h2--left ok-col__h"} -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading ok-h2 ok-h2--left ok-col__h" id="terms">What Are the Four Terms of Study?</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"ok-copy"} -->
<p class="ok-copy">The programme spans four eighteen-week terms structured around key hotel divisions. Term 1 runs from September to January of year one, concentrating on front desk and reservations. Term 2 runs from February to June, dedicating eighteen weeks to banquet and restaurant floor operations. In year two, Term 3 covers the teaching kitchen and rooms division from September to January. Finally, Term 4 runs from February to June, comprising a sixteen-week placement at one of our thirty-eight partner hotels followed by an intensive two-week leadership seminar back on campus. Each term builds progressive operational mastery across every core department.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>
<!-- /wp:group --></section>
<!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:group {"tagName":"section","align":"full","className":"ok-body","layout":{"type":"default"}} -->
<section class="wp-block-group alignfull ok-body"><!-- wp:group {"className":"ok-col","layout":{"type":"default"}} -->
<div class="wp-block-group ok-col"><!-- wp:heading {"level":2,"className":"ok-h2 ok-h2--left ok-col__h"} -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading ok-h2 ok-h2--left ok-col__h">How Are Students Assessed for the Diploma?</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"ok-copy"} -->
<p class="ok-copy">Assessment for the Two-year Diploma in Hotel Operations is based on practical floor evaluations, operational logs, and academic coursework. In each term, instructors evaluate students on technical competence, punctuality, guest communication, and adherence to professional standards during live service at Okami House. Practical assessments are complemented by written examinations in hotel administration and department management. In Term 4, partner hotel supervisors and placement coordinator Rahul Mehta assess student performance during the sixteen-week industry placement. To graduate, students must demonstrate supervisory competence across all four operational divisions and complete the concluding two-week leadership seminar successfully.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>
<!-- /wp:group --></section>
